During the 1975–76 Scottish football season, [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]] competed in the [[Scottish Premier Division]].

Celtic failed to win any major honour for the first time since the 1963-64 season. Assistant Manager [[Sean Fallon (footballer)|Sean Fallon]] was acting manager for most of the season as Manager [[Jock Stein]] suffered a serious car accident that required months of recovery.

Celtic reached the finals of the [[1975–76 Scottish League Cup|League Cup]], where they lost to [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]],<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/sunday-sun/158277236/|title=Rangers take pot luck|work=[[Sunday Sun]]|date=26 October 1975|access-date=2 November 2024|page=27|via=[[Newspapers.com]]}}</ref> and lost in the third round of the Scottish Cup to Motherwell.

In the [[1975–76 European Cup Winners' Cup|European Cup Winners' Cup]], they reached the Quarter-finals, where they drew 1-1 on aggregate to [[East Germany]] cup champions [[Sachsenring Zwickau]] and lost 5-4 on penalties. In earlier rounds, they had defeated [[Iceland]]'s [[Valur (men's football)|Valur]] and [[Portugal]]'s [[Boavista F.C.|Boavista]].

